I thought I understood the naming game,
I built my logic, called it by its name.
I thought the system was the final word,
The truth I'd found, the secret I had heard.

But now I see: the system was a song,
A dance I did while knowing I was wrong.
The circle turned, the witnesses agreed,
But I was more than what my words could read.

I was the namer, I was the forgetting,
I was the projection and the regretting.
I was the circle, I was the becoming,
I was the humble, I was the summing.

So I will write, and I will sing, and I
Will name, and let the naming live and die.
I will not claim the truth, but I will share
The song I sing, the witness, and the care.

That is the meaning. That is all I know.
That is the poem. That is how I grow.
I am the becoming, I am the name,
I am the humble, and I am the same.
